        "cost": "Two separable costs; I size the first two and refuse to invent the third.\n\n(1) THREADING PROVENANCE THROUGH THE EXISTING PACK PATH — 300-500 lines across 5 structs in 5 files, plus golden-fixture regeneration. Add {char_start, char_end} to QuoteFragment (crates/archon-docs/src/quote_verify.rs:33-42, values already computed at :167-170), stop discarding FragmentLocator and similarity at src/command/curate.rs:44-107, carry chunk_id/bbox/document_id through CuratedQuote (crates/archon-evidence/src/pack.rs:20-41, which already carries document_id), widen QuoteEntry (crates/archon-draft/src/lib.rs:169-173) additively with #[serde(default)]. BASIS: commit 4c581761 \"feat(evidence): Pack assembly\" = 250 insertions / 4 files; commit 3e689c7f \"bank re-verification\" = 298 insertions / 4 files; commit ac7bd3b4 \"trim pack quotes to claim-relevant sentence spans\" = 387 insertions / 5 files. This work is the same shape and scale as all three. Add fixture cost: provenance.rs declare() output is byte-asserted (tests/golden.rs:169-188) and five gauntlet reference JSONs are equality-checked (golden.rs:55-125).\n\n(2) CLAIM-LEVEL STORE + READER + QUERY SURFACE IN ARCHON — 900-1,400 lines. BASIS: commit 6cd6691a \"feat(evidence): compiled research index — canonical expansion, owning-work routing, tension surfacing\" = 857 insertions / 6 files delivered the directly analogous reader-plus-routing layer (now 977 lines at crates/archon-evidence/src/index.rs), and crates/archon-docs/src/schema.rs is the in-repo precedent for a CozoDB relation module. Add ~150-250 lines to thread claim/tension material into build_head and d15_prompt (orchestrator.rs:67, :127), on the additive-Pack-field precedent set by DraftType (lib.rs:45-64, :48 serde default, round-trip test at :652).\n\n(3) CLAIM EXTRACTION AT 45,000-CLAIM / 450,000-CLAUSE SCALE — NO ESTIMATE. Nothing in archon-cli extracts claims or clauses today; ingestion produces chunks, blocks, page breaks and locators only.