        "cost": "**~1,700–2,760 new lines of Rust (most likely ~2,200), plus ~700 test lines, to read all 27 entries into canonical concept/claim/edge/tension records.** Every figure has an in-repo measuring stick.\n\nAnchors measured in archon-cli:\n- `crates/archon-evidence/src/index.rs` = 977 lines (673 code + 304 test, `#[cfg(test)]` at :674) for a reader over 4 record types from 1 JSON shape plus an inverted index and 3 query behaviors. This is the unit of measure; the whole job is ~3–4x it.\n- `crates/archon-docs/src/schema.rs` = 644 lines for ~15 Cozo relations incl. an HNSW template → ~43 lines/relation.\n- `crates/archon-knowledge/src/schema.rs` = 211 lines; `run_create` additive-or-ignore at :149–159 is reused, not rewritten.\n- `scripts/compile-corpus-index.py:195–773` = 579 Python lines doing exactly the markdown ontology scraping that must be replaced for the non-JSON entries.\n\nBreakdown:\n- **A. `corpus_*` Cozo schema — 400–650 lines.** Spec §1 names 13 relations + 1 vector relation; 14 × 43 lines/relation ≈ 600.\n- **B. CSV dialect normalizer — 150–250 lines.** Basis: 41 dialects over 219 files / 19,770 rows, 100% name-addressable; a HashMap synonym table (~60 tokens → 10 canonical fields) plus a `csv::Reader` loop. Prior art: `crates/archon-trading/src/ohlcv.rs:96`. NOT 41 adapters.\n- **C. Ontology-JSON adapter, 12 entries — 120–200 lines.** Basis: 11 flat arrays + 1 nested; one serde struct with aliases + 1 special case.\n- **D. Unit/per-chapter payload JSON adapter, 22 entries / 493 files — 400–650 lines.** Basis: 9 recurring payload keys (sections 164 files, concepts 137, interlocutors 135, tensions 133, readings 101, constructs 89, positions 42, claims 31, key_terms 19) × ~50 lines each. The measured 50/53/41 record-shape variance is absorbed by aliases plus `#[serde(flatten)] extra: Map<String,Value>` for the bespoke tail — the top-1 shape already covers 44–61% per key, and the tail is per-entry crown-jewel keys (Burke's `aristotle_exegesis_table`, Calleja's `replaces_prior_construct_table`) that land in `extra` at zero marginal cost, or ~300 lines more if promoted to typed relations.\n- **E. Markdown fallback, 9 entries + Aristotle's 10 `*-ontology.md` — 400–600 lines.** Basis: the incumbent's 579 Python lines cover the same two forms; `pulldown-cmark 0.12` is already a workspace dep (`Cargo.toml:57`), so no regex table-walking.\n- **F. Importer binary + idempotency + row-count verification — 200–350 lines.** Basis: spec §7/P0 with `run_create` reused.\n- **G. Cross-repo path plumbing — 30–60 lines across 3 files.** Basis: `DEFAULT_INDEX_PATH` is a single const at `crates/archon-evidence/src/index.rs:25`, consumed at `src/command/evidence.rs:154` and `:218`; `CompiledIndex::load` is already path-generic; `ARCHON_INDEX_PATH` already exists as a test hook at `index.rs:804`.\n\nTest lines: at the repo's own observed ratio (304/977 ≈ 31%), ~700.\n\n**Per-entry JSON-vs-markdown reduction.** The incumbent spends 579 Python lines on 19 entries ≈ 30 lines/entry for ontology extraction, and that number grows with every new layout. The 12 JSON-twin entries collectively cost ~150 lines of serde ≈ 12 lines/entry, and that number does **not** grow with entry count. Net: 12 of 21 ontology-markdown files (~57% of the scraping surface) disappear, and it is the high-payload 57% — GM 56 nodes, Boredom Secondary 68, VR Pedagogy 60, In-Game 44, RM 39, Uncomfortable 36, Heidegger & Rhetoric 36 = 339 of ~700 nodes move from regex to typed deserialization.\n\nWhat this estimate does NOT cover, and it dwarfs the above: generating the remaining ~42,700 claims and ~450,000 clause records from the 224 ingested documents. No line estimate is offered for that here because nothing in either repo is comparable prior work — an honest unknown rather than an invented number."
