        "cost": "Legacy-view producer swap only (the question in scope): ~350-450 Rust lines in archon + ~150 Python lines for the differ + ZERO TypeScript lines.\n\nBasis, itemized against real code rather than intuition:\n- Serialize derives + emitter: the four structs already exist as Deserialize at crates/archon-evidence/src/index.rs:36-104 (69 lines) — a derive change, not authoring. The write path has a working precedent at crates/archon-evidence/src/pack.rs:239-255 (17 lines: create_dir_all + to_string_pretty + \"\\n\"). Estimate ~200-300 impl lines.\n- Logic to port from Python: 94 lines total — build_canonical_terms (compile-corpus-index.py:1285-1304, 20 lines, the (-len, lower) sort), deduplicate_ontology_nodes (:1311-1357, 47 lines, the name-keyed merge with \"; \"-joined text and sorted alias/unit unions), and main's emit (:1360-1386, 27 lines).\n- Entry-ordering table: 19 TEXT_DIRS keys (compile-corpus-index.py:37-128) transcribed as data, ~40 lines.\n- Tests: ~150 lines, anchored by one round-trip test (read the frozen artifact, emit, assert byte-identical) that subsumes the entire contract.\n- Differ: ~150 Python lines, reusing verbatim the assertions I ran in this session.\n\nComparable prior work in the same crate, as the calibration anchor: crates/archon-evidence/src/index.rs is 674 impl + 302 test lines (mod tests at :675) and delivers the strictly larger job — parse plus greedy longest-match expansion plus tension surfacing plus owning-work routing, with 14 tests including two #[ignore] real-index integration tests. crates/archon-evidence/src/pack.rs is 259 impl + 189 test (mod tests at :260). An emitter that reverses an already-written parser sits comfortably below both.\n\nConfidence: high on the emitter, because the contract is fully pinned (one key order per record type, all-string scalars, no nulls, two explicit sort rules) and the parsing half already exists and passes tests.\n\nExplicitly NOT in this figure and not inferable from it: the claim/clause extraction over 226 documents, and the archon-draft QuoteEntry provenance gap. Both are unestimated above and would dominate any total."
